<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut A-960 bunker fuel prices from Ras Tanura and Dammam by $1.50 to $102.50 tonne ($15.73 a barrel) with effect May 1, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 from the Red Sea ports of Jeddah and Yanbu is $2.50 lower at $97.50 a tonne ($14.97).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the two Gulf ports is $1 lower at $213 a tonne and $1.50 lower from the Red Sea at $192.50.</p>
</text>
